.el .ds Aq '
.TH garuda-toolbox 1  "garuda-toolbox 6.3.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox \- Maintain and configure Garuda Linux and other Arch based systems.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox\fR [\fB\-\-page\fR \fIPAGE\fR] [\fB\-\-action\fR \fIACTION\fR] [\fB\-\-setup\-assistant\fR] [\fB\-\-boot\-repair\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Maintain and configure Garuda Linux and other Arch based systems.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-page\fR \fI<PAGE>\fR
Open the window on this page (see `garuda\-toolbox pages`)
.TP
\fB\-\-action\fR \fI<ACTION>\fR
Run this action of the page once it is open (for example a report on the diagnostics page)
.TP
\fB\-\-setup\-assistant\fR
Open the window on the Setup Assistant
.TP
\fB\-\-boot\-repair\fR
Show Boot Repair on an installed system too, for testing it. The helper still refuses to write to a disk the running system uses
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-status(1)
Show what needs attention: updates, files to merge, health, restart
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-pages(1)
List the pages of the window, for `\-\-page`
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-setup(1)
List and pick the Setup Assistant\*(Aqs apps
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-toggle(1)
List and switch Components, Gaming, System Tweaks and the Setup Assistant
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-apps(1)
List, install and remove the apps of the App Catalog
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-packages(1)
Search, show, install and remove the packages of the repositories and the AUR
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-services(1)
List, start, stop and enable services, the system\*(Aqs and your own
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-kernels(1)
List, install and remove kernels and their headers
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-dkms(1)
Show and build the DKMS modules of each kernel
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-locales(1)
Turn locales on or off and set the system language
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-users(1)
Add, change and remove accounts
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-groups(1)
Add and remove groups
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-configs(1)
Show and edit config files, the system\*(Aqs and your own
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-network(1)
Show the connection and switch radios, drivers and network tests
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-boot(1)
Set the boot menu: default entry, timeout, kernel parameters, looks
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-update(1)
Update the system now, and the AUR packages with `\-\-aur`
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-maintenance(1)
List and run the tasks and repairs of the Maintenance page
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-diagnostics(1)
Collect a report for a forum post or a bug report
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-bootrepair(1)
Repair the boot of an installed system, from the live ISO
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-settings(1)
Show and change the app\*(Aqs own settings
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-doctor(1)
Check what the toolbox needs and say what is missing or broken
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-guide(1)
Read the user guide in the terminal
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-queue(1)
Queue changes as the window does, then apply them as one plan. While the window runs, its own queue
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-completions(1)
Print the completion hook for a shell, which asks this program for the names at each Tab
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-help(1)
Explain a command of this program
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  garuda\-toolbox                          open the window
  garuda\-toolbox \-\-page maintenance       open the window on a page
  garuda\-toolbox status                   what needs attention
  garuda\-toolbox update \-\-yes             update the system without asking

Exit codes:
  0    success      done
  1    failure      a change or a read failed
  2    usage        the arguments were wrong
  3    declined     you answered no
  4    needs\-yes    no terminal to ask on, pass \-\-yes
  5    unavailable  not available on this system
  6    denied       the password dialog or the helper turned it down
  8    page\-rule    refused by the page\*(Aqs rules
  9    attention    status or doctor found something that needs attention
  129  hung\-up      SIGHUP stopped it, as Ctrl+C does
  130  interrupted  Ctrl+C stopped it
  143  terminated   SIGTERM stopped it, as Ctrl+C does
.SH VERSION
v6.3.0
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBGARUDA_TOOLBOX_PAGER\fR
The pager for lists and shows on a terminal, ahead of \fBPAGER\fR. It is split into words without a shell. Empty or \fBcat\fR prints directly.
.TP
\fBPAGER\fR
The pager when \fBGARUDA_TOOLBOX_PAGER\fR is unset. Without either, \fBless \-FRX\fR.
.TP
\fBLESS\fR
Given to the pager as \fBFRX\fR when unset, so less keeps the colours and quits at once when the text fits one screen.
.TP
\fBLV\fR
Given to the pager as \fB\-c\fR when unset, for lv.
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
Any value but an empty one leaves colour out, unless \fB\-\-color always\fR, \fBCLICOLOR_FORCE\fR or \fBFORCE_COLOR\fR asks for it.
.TP
\fBCLICOLOR\fR
\fB0\fR leaves colour out, as \fBNO_COLOR\fR does.
.TP
\fBCLICOLOR_FORCE\fR, \fBFORCE_COLOR\fR
A value other than \fB0\fR colours a pipe too.
.TP
\fBTERM\fR
\fBdumb\fR leaves colour and the spinner out.
.TP
\fBCOLUMNS\fR
The terminal\*(Aqs width, which long cells are cut to. \fB\-\-width\fR comes first.
.TP
\fBVISUAL\fR, \fBEDITOR\fR
The editor of \fBconfigs edit\fR, when it is one of micro, nano, vim, nvim, vi, hx, emacs, ne, joe or mcedit. Else the first installed of micro, nano and vi.
.TP
\fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR
Where completion keeps the names of the system for ten seconds, \fI~/.cache\fR without it.
.TP
\fBCOMPLETE\fR
Set by the completion hooks. The program then answers the completion request of that shell and exits.
.TP
\fBGARUDA_TOOLBOX_LOG\fR
Replaces the log level of the settings, in the filter syntax of tracing, such as \fBdebug\fR.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
less(1), pacman(8), paru(8), systemctl(1)
